+GENERAL_CP_ADVICE = """# General competitive-programming guidance
+- If the task is a stdin/stdout program, read input quickly via sys.stdin (e.g. sys.stdin.readline or sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()) and write output with a single join/print where possible.
+- If the task is a method of a given `Solution` class, keep the exact method name, parameters and return type.
+- Avoid deep recursion on large inputs: either raise the limit with sys.setrecursionlimit (and threading stack size if needed) or use an iterative DFS/BFS.
+- Avoid O(n^2) algorithms when n can be up to about 1e5; prefer sorting, prefix sums, hashing, two pointers, binary search, heaps, or DP with good complexity.
+- Be careful with integer division and modulo (use // and the exact modulus required; handle negative numbers as the problem specifies).
+- Consider edge cases: n=1, empty input, all elements equal, duplicates, zeros, negative values, maximum values.
+- Match the exact output format (spacing, newlines, case, precision, trailing content) specified by the problem.
+"""
+
+PHASE1_DESIGN_PROMPT = """# Phase 1: Understand, design and implement
+Analyze the problem carefully:
+1. Identify the target file to edit and the entry point: is it a complete stdin/stdout program, or a method of a `Solution` class (note its exact name and signature)? Look at existing files in the repository to determine this.
+2. Extract the input format, output format, all constraints, and edge cases.
+3. Propose an algorithm and state its time and space complexity; make sure it fits the constraints.
+4. Implement the solution in the target file, with the correct signature and imports.
+Do not create test files inside the repository yet. Make the edits now."""
+
+PHASE2_SAMPLE_TEST_PROMPT = """# Phase 2: Sample tests
+Create scratch test files OUTSIDE the solution file, for example under /tmp/tests/ (do not put them in the repository).
